   code target branched anywhere else still fails inside the generator before any load. Doc corrected.
   The emitter's relocation half needs nothing: target_label (:230-237) already branches on
   ref.target >= target.text, and its non-data branch yields "code + target".
2. The new LDR-D class has no assembly rule. a11_module_emitter.h:286-290 emits adrp, then selects the s-form load when (add & 0xffc00000) == 0xbd400000 and the x-form add otherwise.
   0x3dc00000 falls through to the x-form add, a wrong instruction, not merely a wrong target. It needs a third
   case emitting the double-register load form ldr d<n>, [x<m>, label@PAGEOFF].
   Maintained at patches/a11-scalar-float-module.patch:32-35.
3. Both Mach-O oracles only know scales 1 and 4: test/a11_module_macho_check.py:69 and
   test/a11_aggregate_macho_check.py:70 compute scale = 4 only for 0xBD400000. The
   0x3dc00000 class scales by 8, so the linked-codeword check would silently mis-resolve rather than fail.
