12) In-flight question closed: what the manifest stores for a code target. Nothing, because no code-target
path exists at all. kind 5 LINK_PTR is the only relocation carrying a same-segment target address, and all
four pinned sites encode
one value form, goal_offset = data_arena_offset + target - text_size, asserted below arena_size. Distance
records
(ADRP+ADD, LDR S, LDR D) are unrelated: target_label (a11_module_emitter.h:230-237) resolves them at link
time and they never reach the runtime - emit-signed-gstate-manifest.py emits only slots and pointers, and
ottsel_signed_gstate.cpp names goal_offset only at :122-123 and :261.
Authoritative semantics: the intact runtime linker ptr_link_v3 (out/jak-project/game/kernel/jak1/klink.cpp:188)
writes *Ptr<u32>(seg_base + patch) = seg_base + target, one flat untagged same-segment address with the
record low bits preserved verbatim. The data form is that formula with seg_base = arena - text; the code form
is the same formula with seg_base = offset(segment.code), i.e. offset(code) + target with no - text
subtraction, which is exactly what target_label already returns for a code target. So the generalization is
not a guard relaxation: the Pointer record must carry the raw target (and its segment) and the runtime write
loop must add the code base, because code minus arena is a link-time symbol difference that no C static
initializer can hold, and goal_offset < arena_size cannot hold once code >= arena_size (:90-91).
Measured scope of the pointer relaxation over every code member: 1255 code-target kind-5 records in exactly
six members - default-menu and default-menu-pc (ENGINE), progress-pc, task-control and target-death
(ENGINE+GAME), sage-finalboss (FIN). All are target%8==4, all patches sit in data (patch >= text), and none
are %8==2. default-menu and default-menu-pc (ENGINE and GAME) are flipped by this fix alone; progress-pc,
