=== LDR Q correction (the 0x3dc00000 class was mis-labelled LDR D) ===
Ground truth from a clang + otool probe of /tmp/ottsel-ldr-probe.s (llvm-mc is not installed):
  ldr q0,[x16,#48] -> 0x3dc00e00    ldr d0,[x16,#48] -> 0xfd401a00
  ldr s0,[x16,#48] -> 0xbd403200    ldr b0,[x16,#48] -> 0x3d40c200
  ldr d0,[x16,#8]  -> 0xfd400600
So 0x3dc... is SIMD&FP LDR Q (size=00, opc=11, imm12 scaled by 16), not LDR D (0xfd4..., size=11, opc=01).
The maintained patch had accepted 0x3dc00000 as scalar_double / ldr d, a silent wrong-address bug: the
assembler scales the emitted section-relative @PAGEOFF by 8 for LDR D and by 16 for LDR Q.

Corpus census (read-only scan_distance32 over 518 objects): 0x91000000 add 141535 words in 511 objects;
0xBD400000 ldr-s 28653 words in 347 objects; 0x3DC00000 ldr-q 1149 words in 169 objects. Every one of the
1149 ldr-q targets satisfies target%16==0, (target-text)%16==0 and target+16<=size. The eight signed KERNEL
members carry zero ldr-q records, so the signed KERNEL baseline is unaffected.
Invariant: LDR Q alignment is measured relative to destination.text, because the emitted reference is
<data label> + (target - text) and the assembler scales that section-relative offset by 16.
Genuine gstring.o: text 16384, size 16636, so size-text = 252 = 16*15+12 and data_size&15 == 12; the
16-aligned candidate data_size-16 = 16620 overruns by 16, so the bound must still reject it.

Corrected scale: 16 for 0x3DC00000, 4 for 0xBD400000, 1 otherwise. Applied to scripts/a11-corpus-census.py,
test/a11_module_macho_check.py and test/a11_aggregate_macho_check.py; test/a11_module_test.cpp keeps the LDR D
rejection as an unsupported class and adds a 16-aligned genuine LDR Q acceptance plus unaligned-target and
past-data rejections. Those four files are outer working-tree files that no patch captures.

