=== GAME link-entry findings before any list widening is designed ===
Release policy is measured, not chosen: for all eight KERNEL objects the loader/generator release set equals
(debug_text != 0) at object offset 52, 8/8 (gcommon 16648, gkernel-h 21348, gkernel 17080, pskernel 16944,
dgo-h 16672 nonempty; gstring-h, gstring, gstate 0). The emitter default rejects nonempty debug and
--release-no-debug omits segment 1, so the per-name tables in emit-signed-gstate-manifest.py:41 and the
loader expected_release :65-68 restate that measurement. A GAME release set does not need a 346-name table;
segments[1].source_text_size is already recorded in the signed manifest for both policies.
link() is the real per-module entry: it returns false for any name not in modules[], then requires
(selected == 0 || loaded[selected-1]) at :241, i.e. strict sequential load order. GAME/level modules load out
of order, so widen this contract (plus validate_layout count :142 and the comparison/kernel arrays :145-146)
before a GAME list can exist; widening only the count is not sufficient.
Three separate gates currently reject non-canonical lists and must move together: emit-signed-gstate-manifest.py:24,
test-a11-gstate-loader.py:44 (canonical full or three-module comparison), and signed-module-build-profile.py
(now general). The loader harness compiles and runs ottsel_signed_gstate.cpp host-side as gstate-activation, so
KERNEL-shaped fixtures are provable without a product build, but a GAME-shaped fixture cannot link because GAME
symbol/type resolution is unavailable in that host runtime. A GAME list therefore stays a product-build gate.
