Scope of proof: host-fixture registry shape and loader behavior only. Each lane runs one member at a time through the fixture's own link_and_exec; no GAME
list is activated in a product, no product build or Simulator ran, and single-member activation is not whole-game signed activation. What it establishes
is the signed GAME lane's ordering contract - a member's parents must load before it (at minimum math+vector-h before navigate-h, rpc-h before
load-dgo/ramdisk/gsound) - and that the loader should reject an undefined Symbol::value feeding an indirect call instead of faulting in non-executable
arena memory. The host-IOP-RPC SIGSEGV (gsound here and in full1) stays a separate blocker that must be root-caused before gsound can activate in any
lane.

