2026-09-14 addendum - gsound SIGSEGV (rpc_h_s0_code+2188) root-caused: null ee::iop is a fixture boot-scope gap, not a product defect
==================================================================================
Gate: `df -h / | tail -1` -> 460Gi 12Gi 8.4Gi 59% / (8.4 GiB < 40 GB); `.git/objects/pack/tmp_pack_*` = 0 (zsh "no matches found" is normal).
Product work stays stopped; this addendum is host-only read-only analysis. No harness, config or product file was touched.

1. The crash. 082228 (config/signed-probe-gsound-rpc.json) and 080012 (315-member full lane) fault with an identical frame list:
   pthread_mutex_lock+12 <- std::__1::mutex::lock()+16 <- IOP_Kernel::sif_rpc+72 <- ee::sceSifCallRpc+84 <- RpcCall_wrapper+104
   <- stack_call_arm64+52 <- ottsel_module_rpc_h_s0_code+2188 <- jak1::link_and_exec+112 <- main+4812 <- start+6992.
   threadState: esr "(Data Abort) byte read Translation fault", far = 808 = 0x328, x0 = 808. EXC_BAD_ACCESS/SIGSEGV, KERN_INVALID_ADDRESS at 0x328.

2. Mechanism. x0 is the first mutex argument, so the faulting statement is `((IOP*)nullptr)->kernel.sif_mtx.lock()`:
   out/jak-project/game/system/IOP_Kernel.cpp:466 `IOP_Kernel::sif_rpc`; :473 `ASSERT(async)` (passes); :474 `sif_mtx.lock()` is the first
   statement after the assert, so `this` is null. The RPC was reached from GOAL rpc-h.gc:114 `rpc-buffer-pair` `call` -> `(rpc-call (-> obj rpc-port) ...)`
   at :141, with gsound.gc:17-18 creating `*sound-player-rpc*` (RPC-SOUND-PLAYER=0) and `*sound-loader-rpc*` (RPC-SOUND-LOADER=1);
   lane rpc-h.json seg0 text_size 16384, entry {segment 2, offset 4}.

3. Offset proof (throwaway probe /tmp/ottsel_iop_offset.cpp, `#define private public` then include "game/system/iop_thread.h"):
   `clang++ -std=gnu++20 -arch arm64 -I out/jak-project/ -o /tmp/ottsel_iop_offset /tmp/ottsel_iop_offset.cpp` ->
   sizeof(IOP)=1216, offsetof(IOP,kernel)=592, offsetof(IOP_Kernel,sif_mtx)=216, sum = 808 = 0x328 == far == x0.

4. Why iop is null in the fixture but not in the app. game/sce/sif_ee.cpp:36 `namespace { ::IOP* iop; }` is internal-linkage BSS (zero-init); it is set
   only by LIBRARY_sceSif_register (:88), whose sole caller is game/runtime.cpp:616 (`ee::LIBRARY_sceSif_register(&iop)`), and nulled again by
   LIBRARY_INIT_sceSif (:92, runtime.cpp:760). The fixture's test/a11_gstate_loader_test.cpp has zero `sceSif`/`iop`/`IOP` references (635 lines) and
   scripts/test-a11-gstate-loader.py never registers one, so `ee::iop` is provably nullptr. sceSifCallRpc (:176) then reaches its `#else` branch at :605
   because the h1 host runtime is compiled WITHOUT OTTSEL_IOS - build/h1/build.ninja `game/CMakeFiles/runtime.dir/kernel/common/kscheme.cpp.o`
   DEFINES = -DDISCORD_DYNAMIC_LIB -DFMT_SHARED -DHAVE_USLEEP=1 -DOTTSEL_NO_EMIT -DREPLXX_BUILDING_DLL -DSQLITE_ENABLE_JSON1
   -DSQLITE_ENABLE_RTREE -DSQLITE_THREADSAFE=1 - so it executes `iop->kernel.sif_rpc(...)` at :609, not the `#ifdef OTTSEL_IOS` shim at :185.

5. Not a product path. scripts/build-ios.sh:97 compiles the runtime with `-DOTTSEL_NO_EMIT -DOTTSEL_IOS` and :250 lists game/sce/sif_ee.cpp, so the iOS
   app takes the `#ifdef OTTSEL_IOS` shim at sif_ee.cpp:185 and returns before touching `iop`. The SIGSEGV only lives in the host fixture's boot scope.

6. Classification of the four GAME probe blockers (now complete):
   navigate-h  SIGABRT Ptr.h:40 (missing type `vector`)  -> fixed by dependency order (math+vector-h), 199 PASS
   load-dgo    SIGBUS null Symbol::value                 -> fixed by rpc-h insertion, 190 PASS
   ramdisk     SIGBUS null Symbol::value                 -> fixed by rpc-h insertion, 190 PASS
   gsound      SIGSEGV rpc_h_s0_code+2188                -> null ee::iop fixture boot-scope gap (this addendum); ordering-clean to that boundary
   gsound and the 315-member control produce the same artifact, so gsound is not an ordering or module defect.

7. Remaining product-side item (unchanged). The loader still does not fail closed on an undefined Symbol::value feeding an indirect call:
   out/jak-project/game/kernel/common/ottsel_signed_gstate.cpp:286 resolves every non-type slot with `jak1::intern_from_c(slot.name)`, which interns a
   missing name at value 0; neither validate_layout (:110-155) nor the write loop (:278-296) requires a call-target symbol to resolve nonzero, so the probe
   lane faults in RW arena memory instead of rejecting the module. A gsound lane would additionally need LIBRARY_sceSif_register(&iop) (or a stub IOP).

Scope: host-fixture analysis only. No product build, no Simulator, no product source change, no new lane, no cleanup. No harness/config/product file modified.

