Corrected conclusion. The name->code identity used by the signed profile is not limited to base containers: it
already reaches streamed level code, as byte-identical members of the built level DGOs, keyed by the same member
name. What stops level code today is the consumer, not the data: (a) `scripts/signed-module-build-profile.py`
