## Addendum 2026-09-14 (3) - loader fail-closed gap verified at source (read-only)

In `game/kernel/common/ottsel_signed_gstate.cpp` the activation path cannot reject a missing dependency:
  - `validate_layout()` (:159) checks slot alignment, kind, offset bounds and the three pinned bootstrap Type counts;
    it never requires a symbol slot to resolve to a nonzero value.
  - the write loop interns unconditionally - `auto sym = jak1::intern_from_c(slot.name);` (:285), then
    `value = ... sym.offset ...` (:288).
  - `intern_from_c` (game/kernel/jak1/kscheme.cpp:1090) calls `find_symbol_from_c` first and, on a miss, allocates a
    NEW symbol whose `value` is never set. A missing name therefore becomes a valid symbol offset carrying value 0,
    and an indirect call through that slot jumps to 0 - the probe SIGBUS/SIGABRT class.
  - entry is registry-name-only: `link()` (:257-258) `while (selected < module_count && std::strcmp(name,
    modules[selected]->name)) ++selected; if (selected == module_count) return false;`, dispatched from
    `link_and_exec` under `OTTSEL_SIGNED_GSTATE_EXPERIMENT` (klink.cpp:936-940).
Fix shape implied by the evidence: resolve symbol slots through a find-only path and fail closed (return false) when the
name is absent, instead of interning at value 0.

Scope: host read-only; no build, no Simulator, no product or harness file touched.

## Addendum 2026-09-14 (4) - blast radius of the streamed-level unblock is one guard script

Read-only trace of the signed lane in `scripts/build-ios.sh`:
