    module-level `for name in dict.fromkeys(['gcommon',*names]): locate_member(name)` loop runs for every action, so
    that script is the single container-shaped guard on the lane.
  - the per-name emission (`:330`-`335`) reads `out/jak1/obj/<name>.o` directly and never consults a container, and the
    debug-policy flag is derived from that object's own segment-1 size, so emitting a level member needs no container
    change at all.
  - `emit-signed-module-arena.py`, `emit-signed-gstate-manifest.py` and the runtime `validate_layout` take arbitrary
    ordered name lists and carry no container or KERNEL-name assumptions.
  - the shell already installs `iso_data/DGO/{TIT,VI1}.DGO` (`build-ios.sh:411`), the two containers holding all 14
    route members, so the installed bundle needs no change for title -> village1.
So: widen `read_container`/`locate_member` in `scripts/signed-module-build-profile.py` to open the level DGOs, add the 14
names to the module list, and pair it with the fail-closed resolution fix in addendum 3. No emitter, arena or bundle
change is implied. All of it remains build-gated (9.1 GiB free, zero tmp packs).

